# Deferred Tools Loading

Use only tool names exposed by the current Antigravity CLI runtime. Load a schema
through the platform's native discovery surface before the first deferred call.
If discovery does not expose a requested tool, stop that route with an
unsupported-tool diagnostic; never substitute a primitive from another agent
platform.

Antigravity supports multiagent workflows. Vendor feature availability does not
prove that this session exposes an integrated ADK execution path. For explicit
`--team`, require both the current runtime schema and a verified ADK mapping for
the requested native team lifecycle. If either is unavailable, stop with an
unsupported-mode diagnostic that identifies the missing capability or mapping.
Do not substitute ordinary subagent execution for an explicit team request.
Do not emit Claude-specific team primitives or guessed team creation, messaging,
or deletion calls. Do not automatically invoke a vendor workflow command based
only on documentation; validate the installed surface and execution contract.
